{# <twig:c975LUi:FlipCard:FlipCard [id=""] [title=""] [level="h2"] [content=""] [backTitle=""] [backContent=""] [media="{{ [frontMedia, backMedia] }}"] [ratio="free"] [class=""] /> #}
{# "media" is an ordered collection/array holding at most two images: the first is the front face's, the second the back's #}
{% set level = level|default('h2') %}
{# Matched against the closed list, not interpolated: the value comes from stored block data and must not write any class name (same rule as the accent in blocks/FlipCard.html.twig). "free" declares none, and the card keeps the height of its tallest face. See FlipCardType::RATIO_CHOICES, whose values these are #}
{% set ratioClass = ratio|default('free') in ['2-3', '3-4', '9-16', '1-1', '3-2', '4-3', '16-9', '21-9', 'credit-card'] ? 'flip-card-ratio-' ~ ratio : '' %}
{% set mediaList = media|default([]) %}
{% set frontMedia = mediaList[0]|default(null) %}
{% set backMedia = mediaList[1]|default(null) %}
{# Two faces are what makes this kind: with nothing at all on the back there is nothing to turn to, so it renders as the plain card it actually is rather than as a card with a control revealing an empty side #}
{% set hasBack = backTitle|default('') or backContent|default('') or backMedia %}
{# The turn is a decoration the eye follows, so it is announced by the accessible name of the control that did it, not by an aria-state on a container: "Voir le verso" and "Voir le recto" say which side is up between them, and focus follows the face that just came up (see flip-card.js) #}
{% set showBack = 'label.flip_card_show_back'|trans({}, 'ui') %}
{% set showFront = 'label.flip_card_show_front'|trans({}, 'ui') %}
{# The fold is the stylesheet's, so the card is painted in shape rather than collapsing into it once the module has loaded, and the one case needing it undone - no JS at all, where the toggles below stay hidden and the back face would sit behind a rotation nothing can undo - is undone from that same stylesheet, under "@media (scripting: none)" (see sass/_flip-card.scss). It used to be a style element wrapped in a noscript and written here, which no validator accepts: a style element is metadata content, invalid anywhere but the head, and this markup is rendered mid-page #}
<div class="flip-card {{ ratioClass }} {{ class|default('') }}"{% if id|default('') %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}{% if hasBack %} data-controller="flipCard"{% endif %}>
    <div class="flip-card-inner">
        <div class="flip-card-face flip-card-front" data-flipCard-target="face">
            {% if title|default('') %}<{{ level }} class="flip-card-title">{{ title }}</{{ level }}>{% endif %}
            <div class="flip-card-body">
                {% if frontMedia %}
                    <p class="flip-card-media"><img src="{{ vich_uploader_asset(frontMedia) }}" alt="{{ frontMedia.alt }}" class="flip-card-img {{ frontMedia.cssClasses|join(' ') }}"{% if frontMedia.intrinsicWidth %} width="{{ frontMedia.intrinsicWidth }}"{% endif %}{% if frontMedia.intrinsicHeight %} height="{{ frontMedia.intrinsicHeight }}"{% endif %} loading="lazy"></p>
                {% endif %}
                {# A <div>, not a <p>: raw Trix HTML is already block-level and a <p> would be split #}
                {% if content|default('') %}<div class="flip-card-text">{{ content|raw|nl2br }}</div>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {% if hasBack %}
                {# The whole face is the control: this fills it, under the content, which is pointer-transparent so a click anywhere lands here - see sass/_flip-card.scss. Hidden until flip-card.js takes over: without it the two faces stay in normal flow, one under the other, and a control turning nothing would be a dead one #}
                <button type="button" class="flip-card-toggle" data-action="flipCard#toggle" aria-label="{{ showBack }}{% if title|default('') %} : {{ title }}{% endif %}" hidden></button>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% if hasBack %}
            <div class="flip-card-face flip-card-back" data-flipCard-target="face">
                {% if backTitle|default('') %}<{{ level }} class="flip-card-title">{{ backTitle }}</{{ level }}>{% endif %}
                <div class="flip-card-body">
                    {% if backMedia %}
                        <p class="flip-card-media"><img src="{{ vich_uploader_asset(backMedia) }}" alt="{{ backMedia.alt }}" class="flip-card-img {{ backMedia.cssClasses|join(' ') }}"{% if backMedia.intrinsicWidth %} width="{{ backMedia.intrinsicWidth }}"{% endif %}{% if backMedia.intrinsicHeight %} height="{{ backMedia.intrinsicHeight }}"{% endif %} loading="lazy"></p>
                    {% endif %}
                    {% if backContent|default('') %}<div class="flip-card-text">{{ backContent|raw|nl2br }}</div>{% endif %}
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="flip-card-toggle" data-action="flipCard#toggle" aria-label="{{ showFront }}{% if backTitle|default('') %} : {{ backTitle }}{% endif %}" hidden></button>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
